# TASK-260715-2rcvr0 runtime verification notes

## Question

What does the implemented M1 runtime own and report, and which boundaries are
actually available for M2–M5 without moving authority into the host app?

## Verified implementation facts

- `TunnelRuntimeCoordinator` performs configuration, SSH, TCP, safe-DNS,
  resource-free packet preparation, settings apply, packet activation, health,
  snapshot publication, and reverse cleanup in the documented order.
- Its only usable M1 state publishes `connectedDegraded`, TCP and safe DNS true,
  UDP false. No full-mode inference exists.
- `TunnelProviderAdapter` owns generation, callback, deadline, cleanup, request
  ledger, and provider-failure semantics. Legacy version discovery is
  phase-independent; v1 commands require a running generation and fresh UUID.
- `RuntimeDiagnosticsStore` is fixed-cardinality, generation-scoped, bounded to
  256 pending updates, and rejects unknown labels without retaining them.
- `VPNSessionController.retire()` cancels app-side observation and requests but
  never calls `stopTunnel()`. The provider remains system-owned.
- `MacOSProductionDependencyFactory` validates the exact M0 binding before any
  component factory and constructs one fresh graph per generation.
- The checked-in `ReluxProxyMacTunnel.PacketTunnelProvider` remains a shell and
  does not instantiate that factory/root. iOS production target work is
  deferred. Build evidence is therefore not live-runtime-wiring evidence.

## Negative and boundary evidence reviewed

- M0 production composition tests distinguish absent from unreadable input and
  reject digest/semantic narrowing before component construction at
  `MacOSProductionDependencyFactory.makeRuntime`.
- M1 ingress tests admit TCP and virtual-DNS TCP/UDP but reject general UDP as
  deferred at `M1PrivateIngressDispatcher`.
- Message tests reject missing/duplicate/stale request IDs, unsupported
  versions/kinds/values, duplicate keys, excessive nesting, malformed UTF-8,
  oversized input, and non-running command routing at
  `TunnelProviderAdapter.handleAppMessage`.
- Diagnostics tests pass prohibited values through the production diagnostic
  update/snapshot surfaces and require their absence; unknown metric/error
  names are rejected and counted.
- Harness configuration negative tests own independent accepted/rejected bounds
  and traverse `HarnessApplication.run`; all mandatory failure scenarios use
  exact nonzero exits.

## Board completeness

No new story, task, dependency, research task, or beyond-spec behavior was
created. The existing task is one atomic documentation deliverable and already
depends on the three completed prerequisites that define runtime behavior,
diagnostics, and migration isolation. M2–M5 links are handoff references, not
new dependencies. The provider-shell discrepancy is an implemented-state
anomaly to document, not authorization to wire the target in this task.


